{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-8788-1",
  "summary": "clamav vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that ClamAV incorrectly handled certain zip archive\nfiles. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause ClamAV\nto crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-20337,\nCVE-2026-20338)\n\nIt was discovered that ClamAV incorrectly handled certain PESpin files.\nA remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause ClamAV to\ncrash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-20339)\n\nIt was discovered that ClamAV incorrectly handled certain GPT files. A\nremote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause ClamAV to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-20345)\n\nIt was discovered that ClamAV incorrectly handled certain PDF files. A\nremote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause ClamAV to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-20346)\n\nIt was discovered that ClamAV incorrectly handled certain Mach-O files.\nA remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause ClamAV to\ncrash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-20347)\n\nIt was discovered that ClamAV incorrectly handled certain XAR files. A\nremote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause ClamAV to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-20348)",
